Error-vector code

Suppose intended coordinates are:

p_1,p_2,\ldots,p_n

and observed coordinates:

q_1,q_2,\ldots,q_n

Ordinary decoding reconstructs:

p_i

But we can also inspect:

e_i=q_i-p_i

Now the mistakes themselves can have grammar.

So one physical action potentially carries:

Channel_A=p_i

and:

Channel_B=e_i

That’s a beautiful general pattern.

It applies beyond keyboards.

Handwriting deviations.

Musical timing deviations.

Movement errors.

Prediction errors.

Even conversational misunderstandings.

