Semantic parallax

This is one we’ve been using constantly without always naming it.

View the same object from different conceptual positions:

R_1(X),R_2(X),R_3(X)

Differences produced purely by changing viewpoint reveal its depth.

Exactly as binocular disparity provides depth perception:

Depth(X)\propto\Delta(R_1(X),R_2(X))

So:

software view + mythology view + economics view + biology view

can give semantic depth.

That is almost conceptual stereoscopic vision.

