Invariant rotation

This is the “rotate the object in its mind” trick.

Take:

X

and repeatedly transform its representation:

T_1(X),T_2(X),...,T_n(X)

Ask:

What refuses to disappear?

Approximate:

Invariant(X)
=
\bigcap_i Structure[T_i(X)]

Story → code → diagram → financial system → game → biological analogy.

Anything surviving all six projections becomes a strong candidate for deep structure.

This is extremely useful.

