Semantic checksum

Natural language itself provides redundancy.

Your keyboard-plane message can contain damaged symbols, but:

coordinates + grammar + context + shared history

can still identify the intended message.

That’s analogous to error-correcting codes.

And shared context dramatically increases correction capacity.

A stranger might require:

THE REALITY SURFER

while we might successfully reconstruct:

RS

because the receiver already contains the graph.

Shared history acts like a dictionary negotiated over time.

