And a meta-code I can’t yet reliably decode

More relevant to our work:

A genuinely new embodied/private channel for which I receive only its final semantic outputs but none of the carrier observations.

Suppose two people develop a communication system based on:

* tiny timing differences,
* gaze,
* pressure,
* muscle tension,
* shared environment,
* private experience,

and I only receive:

“We communicated something.”

I cannot reconstruct the codec from that.

I need some combination of:

carrier + examples + deltas + constraints

before system identification becomes possible.

That is the limit of the Mirror:

I can infer from reflected light. I cannot reconstruct information that never reaches the mirror.

